# Runtime OpenXR wire-protocol ABI pin.
#
# The DisplayXR OpenXR extension headers vendored under
#   Source/DisplayXRCore/Private/Native/openxr/XR_DXR_*.h
# are copied VERBATIM from DisplayXR/displayxr-runtime at the commit below.
# The `abi-guard` CI job (.github/workflows/lint.yml) fetches those headers at
# this ref and fails the build if the vendored copies have drifted — that drift
# is what caused the black-window regression (the Win32 window-binding struct
# grew fields the plugin's hand-mirror lacked) and the rendering-mode stride
# bug (#234).
#
# To adopt new runtime protocol: set this SHA to the new runtime commit, re-copy
# every XR_DXR_*.h header listed in the abi-guard job from displayxr-runtime at
# that SHA into Source/DisplayXRCore/Private/Native/openxr/, and rebuild. Keep
# this as a full 40-char commit SHA (immutable) — not a branch name.
#
# The pin is intentionally independent of the runtime's versions.json co-release
# matrix: this plugin is a downstream consumer of the wire protocol, released on
# its own cadence. This file is the only coupling between the two repos.

# runtime#803 (display-zones spec v3: per-zone cosmetic feather).
#
# Adopted for XR_DXR_display_zones — the sole region paradigm since ADR-031 and
# the canvas source for the runtime's weave-to-texture editor-preview path
# (issue #38). Diff vs the previous v2.0.0 pin on the five headers already
# vendored: comments and SPEC_VERSION values only, no struct or ABI change.
# SPEC_VERSION numbers jump (view_rig 1 -> 3, win32_window_binding 1 -> 8,
# display_info 1 -> 16, atlas_capture 1 -> 3, cocoa 1 -> 6) because runtime#738
# restored the pre-rename XR_EXT_* numbering; this is exactly why extension
# support is gated on the NAME and never on SPEC_VERSION.
